  {
   "id": "b2",
   "function": "problem",
   "scene_type": "zlx_cutaway",
   "spoken": "The measurement uses a standardised single-cylinder test engine, the CFR engine. Its special feature: the compression ratio can be adjusted while it runs. So you can raise it until the fuel starts to knock. That point is what counts. Everything else is kept the same.",
