  {
   "id": "b5",
   "function": "insight",
   "scene_type": "zlx_board",
   "spoken": "There are two test methods. For the research octane number, the engine runs at six hundred rpm with intake air at fifty-two degrees. For the motor octane number, it runs at nine hundred rpm and a hundred and forty-nine degrees. The research number is always higher. At pumps in the US, by the way, the sign shows the average of the two.",
